.TH NOLINEMAP 1 "" "noweb contrib"
.SH NAME
nolinemap \- map messages about tangled files back to noweb sources
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nolinemap
[\fB\-L\fP \fIfmt\fP]
[\fB\-c\fP \fIleader\fP]
[\fB\-\-\fP]
[\fIcommand\fP [\fIarg\fP ...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I nolinemap
reads the output of a compiler, interpreter, linter, or any other
tool, finds references to files tangled by
.IR notangle (1),
and rewrites them so that they point into the noweb sources, using
the location comments inserted by the
.IR linemark (1)
filter.
It also understands #line directives, so it serves
.B notangle \-L
output as well.
It recognizes Python tracebacks and \fIfile\fP:\fIline\fP[:\fIcolumn\fP]
references; columns are translated too, by comparing the indentation
of the tangled line and its source line.
References to files that do not exist or contain no markers pass
through untouched.
.PP
With a
.IR command ,
nolinemap runs it, translates both its standard output and standard
error, and exits with the command's exit status, so it can wrap
commands in a Makefile transparently.
Without one it translates standard input, for use in a pipe.
.PP
nolinemap is also installed under the alias
.IR noerr ,
after the older Perl program it supersedes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-L \fIfmt\fP
The marker format that was used when tangling; see
.IR linemark (1).
The default is
.BR "# %L \(dq%F\(dq" .
.TP
.B \-c \fIleader\fP
The comment leader that was given to
.B linemark \-c
when tangling.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print a help message and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
notangle -Rfoo.py -filter linemark foo.nw > foo.py
nolinemap python3 foo.py
make 2>&1 | nolinemap
.fi
.SH BUGS
A hand-written comment that happens to match the marker format
exactly is indistinguishable from a marker and skews the mapping
until the next real marker.
Column translation counts a tab as one column.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR linemark (1),
.IR notangle (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Daniel Bosk <dbosk@kth.se>
